    "answerHtml": "<p>Inventory valuation assigns supported costs to the units sold and the stock still held. FIFO, weighted average and specific identification can allocate the same purchase cost differently. First establish the accounting framework and inventory record; then reconcile cost of goods sold plus ending inventory to the total available cost.</p>",
