    "scopeBoundary": "Owns role definition, recruitment channels, consistent selection and onboarding measurement; complements rather than duplicates the cost-per-hire and employee-cost calculators.",
    "opening": "A recruitment strategy connects a real workload gap with a defined role, a fair selection process and a funded onboarding plan. Choose channels by qualified outcomes and delivery readiness, not applicant volume alone. Measure hiring expense separately from the recurring cost and capacity of the person who joins.",
    "answerHtml": "<p>A recruitment strategy connects a real workload gap with a defined role, a fair selection process and a funded onboarding plan. Choose channels by qualified outcomes and delivery readiness, not applicant volume alone. Measure hiring expense separately from the recurring cost and capacity of the person who joins.</p>",
    "answerTitle": "Quick answer",
