    "primaryKeyword": "payroll small business",
    "scopeBoundary": "Owns the payroll record-to-payment workflow and wage/liability reconciliation; total reward design, recruitment strategy and employer-cost pricing remain separate owners.",
    "opening": "Payroll is the controlled process of recording work, calculating authorized pay, applying supported deductions and employer costs, paying employees and reconciling liabilities and filings. Gross wages, take-home pay and total employer cost are different amounts. Use current federal, state and local requirements for actual payroll; the examples below demonstrate records and reconciliation, not tax withholding calculations.",
    "answerHtml": "<p>Payroll is the controlled process of recording work, calculating authorized pay, applying supported deductions and employer costs, paying employees and reconciling liabilities and filings. Gross wages, take-home pay and total employer cost are different amounts. Use current federal, state and local requirements for actual payroll; the examples below demonstrate records and reconciliation, not tax withholding calculations.</p>",
    "answerTitle": "Quick answer",
